{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01030",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 10.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.47,
      "end_seconds": 15.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 16.81,
      "end_seconds": 20.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.59,
      "end_seconds": 25.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "So, please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.86,
      "end_seconds": 33.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Doctor, it's an itchy painful right ear. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.15,
      "end_seconds": 38.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Okay, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.96,
      "end_seconds": 43.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "It's been two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.01,
      "end_seconds": 53.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.37,
      "end_seconds": 72.87,
      "duration_seconds": 17.5,
      "text": "I mean, I'd give it a eight, out of ten. Honestly, all the time. Touching the ear and lying on it definitely sets it off. And there's pain when I move my jaw as well, three days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.19,
      "end_seconds": 78.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.56,
      "end_seconds": 85.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "I notice it more with chewing. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.5,
      "end_seconds": 92.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Have you had an itchy painful right ear before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.64,
      "end_seconds": 100.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 101.47,
      "end_seconds": 105.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 106.7,
      "end_seconds": 115.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 127 over 82, temperature 36.6. Pulse is 72 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.67,
      "end_seconds": 119.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.97,
      "end_seconds": 126.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.18,
      "end_seconds": 143.88,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.47,
      "end_seconds": 147.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.61,
      "end_seconds": 167.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "The ear canal is red and swollen with some debris, and pulling the ear hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.36,
      "end_seconds": 171.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.2,
      "end_seconds": 187.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "I can't see the eardrum properly because of the swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.23,
      "end_seconds": 189.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.35,
      "end_seconds": 202.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Any swelling behind the ear, fever or recent cold at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.78,
      "end_seconds": 217.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "No, no swelling behind the ear, no fever, no recent cold. I did have muffled hearing on that side at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.27,
      "end_seconds": 224.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Has there been any dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.32,
      "end_seconds": 226.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nope, no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 228.97,
      "end_seconds": 233.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.83,
      "end_seconds": 240.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.89,
      "end_seconds": 248.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Has there been any ringing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.17,
      "end_seconds": 252.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no ringing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.99,
      "end_seconds": 256.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.44,
      "end_seconds": 260.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, um, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.63,
      "end_seconds": 265.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.3,
      "end_seconds": 270.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.56,
      "end_seconds": 277.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Okay, what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.23,
      "end_seconds": 283.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia. My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.12,
      "end_seconds": 288.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.47,
      "end_seconds": 294.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 296.34,
      "end_seconds": 300.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 250 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.13,
      "end_seconds": 305.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.47,
      "end_seconds": 314.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.35,
      "end_seconds": 323.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.26,
      "end_seconds": 329.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about ten years. I have eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.91,
      "end_seconds": 334.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.96,
      "end_seconds": 347.25,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.06,
      "end_seconds": 358.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.89,
      "end_seconds": 362.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.35,
      "end_seconds": 366.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.32,
      "end_seconds": 369.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, you know, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.89,
      "end_seconds": 389.02,
      "duration_seconds": 18.13,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? My working impression is an outer ear infection. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Another possibility is a wax problem. A middle ear infection is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.0,
      "end_seconds": 393.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Oh, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.34,
      "end_seconds": 427.87,
      "duration_seconds": 32.53,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an outer ear infection. We'll begin with ciprofloxacin ear drops, three times a day, for seven days. That should help with outer ear infection. Keep water out of the ear and don't use cotton buds. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.64,
      "end_seconds": 432.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.24,
      "end_seconds": 441.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.9,
      "end_seconds": 442.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.81,
      "end_seconds": 453.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "See me again if it's not better in four days. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 454.31,
      "end_seconds": 457.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Thank you, you know, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 459.07,
      "end_seconds": 460.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}